        "message" : [
          "%md",
          "",
          "## Narrative",
          "",
          "The red team ground truth shows a few staging hosts that account for many compromise events. An attacker who gains access to one computer uses it as a beachhead to reach many victims, and the pivot can cascade over several hops.",
          "",
          "This analysis profiles the beachhead shape in the ground truth and searches the full cyber graph for computers with the same burst shape. It then isolates new candidates, finds the accounts behind a beachhead, and follows its multi-hop reach.",
          "",
          "**Scope:** the analysis targets loud, high-volume pivots, such as `C17693`. Quiet compromises with few victims are the subject of Scenario 1."
        ],
