          "",
          "## Scope: Quiet Compromises",
          "",
          "The red team labels count at most 2 victims per hour for `C19932` and `C22409`, although both hosts connect to up to 17 computers in an hour. Bursts of that size are common: their best hours rank 6,512 by burst size among 867,238 hourly bursts (Step 3a). Host-to-host fan-out therefore does not separate them from ordinary activity. These two hosts show a different shape: one account persisting quietly on a secondary computer. Scenario 1 detects them (`U737@DOM1` with `C19932`, `U3486@DOM1` with `C22409`)."
