          "",
          "## Findings",
          "",
          "### Finding 1: Same Campaign, Two Angles",
          "",
          "The staging hosts `C17693`, `C19932`, and `C22409` are the same computers that Scenario 1 found as source computers of stolen credentials. Both scenarios describe one connected campaign: by identity (whose credentials were reused) and by host (which computer became a pivot point). The fourth staging host, `C18025`, reached a single victim in three events within minutes.",
          "",
          "### Finding 2: Two Attack Shapes Under One Label",
          "",
          "Only `C17693` fits the shape \"beachhead reused to reach many victims\": 296 victims, with 30 of 73 active hours at 5 or more victims. `C19932` (8 victims) and `C22409` (3 victims) stay at 1 or 2 confirmed victims per hour, although they connect to up to 17 computers in an hour. They show Scenario 1's persistence shape under a Scenario 2 label.",
          "",
          "### Finding 3: Host Fan-Out Does Not Separate Attackers from Normal Activity",
          "",
